{"duration_api_ms":805137,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3e4ed07f-8c56-4e60-8466-7ade3e7f323c","total_cost_usd":8.3960035,"usage":{"input_tokens":150,"cache_creation_input_tokens":189076,"cache_read_input_tokens":9925741,"output_tokens":61419,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":14088},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":189076,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1434,"cache_read_input_tokens":198363,"cache_creation_input_tokens":718,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":718},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":6053,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.006148,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":150,"outputTokens":61419,"cacheReadInputTokens":9925741,"cacheCreationInputTokens":189076,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":8.3898555,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":14088,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01NDyUttGBrtKu7ejTwkrJQg","tool_input":{"command":"D=.temp/TASK-260830-1bipsa\n# Package the review probe as one reproducible artifact, then remove the Go files from the module tree.\nmkdir -p $D/artifact\n{\n  echo \"# TASK-260830-1bipsa review probe — independent attack suite\"\n  echo\n  echo \"Reviewer-authored, out-of-tree. Place under '<repo>/.temp/TASK-260830-1bipsa/probe/'\"\n  echo \"(package 'probe') and run: go test ./.temp/TASK-260830-1bipsa/probe/ -count=1 -v\"\n  echo \"It imports internal/cliresult, internal/axerror and internal/specdoc and drives\"\n  echo \"the real exported entry points. It was NOT committed; the reviewed tree is unchanged.\"\n  echo\n  for f in $D/probe/*_test.go; do\n    echo \"## $(basename $f)\"; echo '```go'; cat \"$f\"; echo '```'; echo\n  done\n} > $D/artifact/probe.md\nwc -l $D/artifact/probe.md\nrm -rf $D/probe $D/s172 $D/cliresult.bak $D/mutants.py $D/*.bak\nls $D; echo \"--- module clean? ---\"; go build ./... && echo \"BUILD OK\"; git status --short; echo \"(clean)\"","timeout":420000,"description":"Package probe artifact and clean module tree"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":76,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Verdict: ACCEPTED.** `CR-TASK-260830-1bipsa-1` rev 1 accepted, element parked at `to-review` for the orchestrator to checkpoint.\n\n## Why the empty delta wasn't an empty producer\n\nThe CR base OID `f34d91d` **is** the leaf commit, so base tree == candidate tree and the patch had zero paths. Real delta is `ebc4e31..f34d91d` — 31 files, +7241/−36. That's the snapshot bug already filed as #113. `HEAD^{tree}` still equals the candidate tree, so what I reviewed is exactly what the CR names.\n\n## Attacked, not read\n\nI wrote an out-of-tree probe package driving the real exported entry points, rather than re-reading the producer's logs.\n\n- **Leaf 1's aliasing defect does not repeat.** Wrote through every caller container at every depth after `New` returned, through `Body()`, `Extension()`, `IDs`, on both the `New` and `Decode` construction paths. Output unchanged everywhere.\n- **Gates held:** `--yes` can't bypass any dropped expectation flag; unrelated flags aren't accepted as expectation flags; exactly 3 surfaces take `--yes`; `rpc serve` refuses `--json` in 4 spellings; second stdout document / human text in JSON mode / prompt under `--non-interactive` all refused writing nothing; ~50 `Decode` wire mutations all refused; takeover adoption correct in all 8 combinations and unskippable by omitting or forging the kind; exit status matches the registry for every registered code through both `ExitStatus` and real `Emit`.\n\n## The two residuals\n\n**R2 closed, derivation real.** I measured 18 rows from the pinned document myself. Four registry mutants, each verified present — including **renumbering 16→18 with the count unchanged** — all RED. Not a count-only pin.\n\n**R1 closed, with one finding.** 7/9/16/63 all RED now (16 and 64 were green before). But the pin works via the literal `!= 8` guard, *not* the boundary fixtures — both fixtures are computed from the constant and slide with it. I proved it: removed the guard, widened to 63, suite went **GREEN**. The test's comment about its own mechanism is false. Not rework — the residual's purpose (a widening must not be silent) is met loudly — but worth correcting.\n\n## Clause claims\n\nAll 8 §14.2 excerpts verified verbatim against the pinned document at their declared lines, all inside 14.2, all RFC 2119. **Wrong-actor check: all 8 govern the ax CLI host** — leaf 1's shape doesn't repeat. §15.2 was *not* re-bound (byte-identical to `ebc4e31`), and 14.2#6 was correctly refused: `internal/cliresult` has zero importers outside itself and the only `os.Exit` calls are cataloggen/tracecheck. The #3-vs-#6 line is coherent — #3 is a writer property over a caller-supplied stream, #6 needs process termination.\n\nProducer evidence reproduced exactly: 13/13 packages green, tracecheck `17/403`, `-section 14.2` red at 8/9, harness 48 killed / 2 subsumed / **0 broken**, coverage 95.3% and 99.7%, every stated ratio measured true.\n\n## Two things for you\n\n**Note for leaf 3:** `Decode` runs the closed-member check *before* the major check, so a future-major document carrying a new top-level member reports `unknown top-level member` with `errors.Is(ErrUnsupportedMajor) = false`. Both paths refuse — no bypass — but §1.6 scopes its fail-closed rule to \"a major version 1 object\", exactly the case where the major should already be settled. Leaf 3 owns that decision.\n\n**Host hygiene, ахпер:** your Go build cache had grown to **134 GB** against 150 MiB free disk — the suite literally couldn't link (`no space left on device`). `go clean -cache` freed 135 GB. Unrelated to this change, but that disk was full-full.\n\nAll production mutations used file backups (never `git checkout` in a story worktree) and every one was restored — tree clean, one signed commit past the checkpoint.","ttft_ms":2208,"type":"result","duration_ms":1236016,"uuid":"993adfd3-30fb-49d5-a4f7-6d7e5857222e","ttft_stream_ms":1262,"time_to_request_ms":51,"queued_turn_count":0}
